# Disable USB autosuspend for the ASUS Xtion / PrimeSense depth camera (1d27:0600).
#
# Why: Linux autosuspends idle USB devices (2s on this host). During the camera
# driver's startup there is a brief gap before all video streams (color/depth/IR) are
# open; if that gap crosses the timer, the kernel suspends the Xtion mid-startup, the IR
# stream fails to open, and the device "disconnects" and re-enumerates. That is the
# intermittent camera-flapping seen at bring-up (works on retry only because a fresh
# enumeration sometimes beats the timer). Keeping the device powered on removes the race.
#
# Install: sudo cp this file to /etc/udev/rules.d/ then reload+trigger (see
# install_xtion_udev.sh). Applies to any Xtion by vendor/product id, so it survives
# reboots and replugs regardless of the USB device number.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="1d27", ATTR{idProduct}=="0600", TEST=="power/control", ATTR{power/control}="on"
